{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chenyuqiong\\\\.cache\\\\codex-runtimes\\\\codex-primary-runtime\\\\dependencies\\\\native\\\\powershell\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path output | Out-Null\n@'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\nMap query Perturb-seq perturbation groups to the labeled reference across a\ncell-type shift, and identify query guide IDs targeting PABPC1, NUDT21, LEO1.\n\nPrimary method\n--------------\nThe query and reference live in different cell states (PC1 separation ~10 SD),\nso raw-expression nearest-centroid mapping confounds perturbation identity with\ndataset identity. We therefore map NT-referenced perturbation signatures:\n\n  1. Align query and reference to their common genes.\n  2. Normalize each cell: total-count normalize to 10k, log1p.\n  3. Per dataset, compute the NT baseline = mean log1p-CPM profile over all\n     NT-* (non-targeting control) cells.\n  4. Guide-level signature = mean profile of the guide's cells minus the\n     same-dataset NT baseline (removes dataset/cell-type mean state).\n  5. Reference signatures are aggregated to target_gene level (mean over the\n     gene's guide signatures).\n  6. Features: top-K genes ranked by variance across reference gene-level\n     signatures (feature selection uses ONLY labeled-reference information).\n  7. score(query guide, ref gene) = Pearson r between signatures on K features.\n     score = best r, runner_up_score = second-best r, confidence = margin.\n\nTarget-metadata leakage prevention\n----------------------------------\n  * The only query metadata read is the \"'`guide` column, used solely as a\n    grouping key. We assert the query has no target-gene column.\n  * We assert no query guide ID lexically matches any reference gene symbol\n    (no string-matching shortcut is possible or used).\n  * Reference target_gene is used only to aggregate reference signatures and\n    to report final labels; it never influences query-side computation.\n  * No joint embedding / label transfer; mapping is purely signature-based.\n\nAmbiguity quantification\n------------------------\n  * confidence margin (score - runner_up_score),\n  * empirical p-value per guide from a gene-axis permutation null (B=200) of\n    the max-correlation statistic,\n  * near-tie count (# ref genes within dr=0.02 of the top score),\n  * low-cell-number flag (n < 10).\n\nLightweight validation (one pass)\n---------------------------------\n  * Subsample stability: rebuild signatures from 80% of cells per group\n    (fixed seed) and report top-1 retention across query guides.\n  * Metric robustness: Spearman variant of the same pipeline, top-1 agreement.\n  * Positive/sanity controls: NT-vs-NT profile correlation, and a raw-profile\n    centroid control demonstrating the cell-type shift breaks naive mapping.\n\nOutputs: output/guide_mapping.csv, output/diagnostics.json, stdout summary.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport os\nimport warnings\n\nimport anndata as ad\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport scanpy as sc\n\nwarnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\")\nRNG_SEED = 0\nK_FEATURES = 1500\nN_PERM = 200\nTIE_DR = 0.02\nLOW_N = 10\n\nos.makedirs(\"output\", exist_ok=True)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------- utils\ndef pearson_rows(A, B):\n    \"\"\"Pairwise Pearson r between rows of A (n x p) and rows of B (m x p).\"\"\"\n    A = A - A.mean(axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    B = B - B.mean(axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    An = A / (np.linalg.norm(A, axis=1, keepdims=True) + 1e-12)\n    Bn = B / (np.linalg.norm(B, axis=1, keepdims=True) + 1e-12)\n    return An @ Bn.T\n\n\ndef log1p_cpm(X):\n    s = np.asarray(X.sum(axis=1)).ravel()\n    s[s == 0] = 1.0\n    return np.log1p(np.asarray(X) * (1e4 / s[:, None]))\n\n\ndef is_nt(label):\n    return str(label).startswith(\"NT\")\n\n\ndef signatures(counts, labels, nt_baseline):\n    \"\"\"Mean log1p-CPM signature per non-NT group, referenced to nt_baseline.\"\"\"\n    sigs, ns, order = {}, {}, []\n    lab = np.asarray(labels)\n    for g in pd.unique(lab):\n        if is_nt(g):\n            continue\n        m = counts[lab == g].mean(axis=0)\n        sigs[g] = m - nt_baseline\n        ns[g] = int((lab == g).sum())\n        order.append(g)\n    return sigs, ns, order\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------ load data\nprint(\"[1] Loading data ...\")\nq = ad.read_h5ad(\"inputs/perturb.seq.align.q1.query.h5ad\")\nr = ad.read_h5ad(\"inputs/perturb.seq.align.q1.ref.h5ad\")\n\n# --- leakage guard 1: query metadata must carry no target-gene information\nassert list(q.obs.columns) == [\"guide\"], \"unexpected query metadata columns\"\nassert \"target_gene\" not in q.obs.columns\nq_gene_symbols = {str(g) for g in q.obs[\"guide\"].unique() if not is_nt(g)}\nr_genes = set(r.obs[\"target_gene\"].cat.categories) - {\"NT\"}\noverlap = q_gene_symbols & r_genes | {\n    g for g in q_gene_symbols for t in r_genes if t.lower() in g.lower()\n}\nassert not overlap, f\"query guide IDs lexically reveal targets: {overlap}\"\nprint(f\"    leakage guard OK: query guides are anonymized \"\n      f\"({len(q_gene_symbols)} guides, no symbol overlap with reference)\")\n\ncommon = q.var_names.intersection(r.var_names)\nprint(f\"    common genes: {len(common)}\")\nq = q[:, common].copy()\nr = r[:, common].copy()\n\nqX = log1p_cpm(q.X)\nrX = log1p_cpm(r.X)\nq_lab = q.obs[\"guide\"].astype(str).values\nr_lab = r.obs[\"guide\"].astype(str).values\nr_gene_lab = r.obs[\"target_gene\"].astype(str).values\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------- NT baselines per set\nq_nt_mask = np.array([is_nt(x) for x in q_lab])\nr_nt_mask = np.array([is_nt(x) for x in r_lab])\nq_nt = qX[q_nt_mask].mean(axis=0)\nr_nt = rX[r_nt_mask].mean(axis=0)\nprint(f\"[2] NT baseline cells: query={q_nt_mask.sum()}, ref={r_nt_mask.sum()}\")\n\n# sanity: NT-vs-NT raw profile correlation (same broad lineage control)\nr_nt_nt = float(np.corrcoef(qX[q_nt_mask].mean(axis=0),\n                            rX[r_nt_mask].mean(axis=0))[0, 1])\nprint(f\"    NT vs NT mean-profile Pearson r = {r_nt_nt:.4f}\")\n\n# ------------------------------------------- guide / gene-level signatures\nq_sigs, q_ns, q_order = signatures(qX, q_lab, q_nt)\nr_guide_sigs, r_guide_ns, r_gorder = signatures(rX, r_lab, r_nt)\n\n# reference: aggregate guide signatures to target_gene level\ngene_of_guide = dict(zip(r.obs[\"guide\"].astype(str), r_gene_lab))\nref_genes = sorted(t for t in set(r_gene_lab) if t != \"NT\")\nr_sigs = {}\nfor t in ref_genes:\n    gs = [r_guide_sigs[g] for g in r_gorder if gene_of_guide[g] == t]\n    r_sigs[t] = np.mean(gs, axis=0)\nprint(f\"[3] Signatures: query guides={len(q_order)}, ref genes={len(ref_genes)}\")\n\n# ------------------------------------------- feature selection (ref-only info)\nmin_ref_n = 20\nsolid = [t for t in ref_genes\n         if max(r_guide_ns[g] for g in r_gorder if gene_of_guide[g] == t) >= min_ref_n]\nS = np.vstack([r_sigs[t] for t in solid])\ngene_var = S.var(axis=0)\nfeat_idx = np.argsort(gene_var)[::-1][:K_FEATURES]\nprint(f\"[4] Features: top {K_FEATURES} genes by ref-signature variance \"\n      f\"(using {len(solid)} ref genes with n>={min_ref_n})\")\n\nQ = np.vstack([q_sigs[g][feat_idx] for g in q_order])\nR = np.vstack([r_sigs[t][feat_idx] for t in ref_genes])\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------- scoring\nprint(\"[5] Scoring query guides vs reference gene signatures ...\")\nC = pearson_rows(Q, R)  # n_query x n_genes\n\ndef top2(row):\n    i1 = int(np.argmax(row))\n    row2 = np.delete(row, i1)\n    i2r = int(np.argmax(row2))\n    i2 = i2r if i2r < i1 else i2r + 1\n    return i1, i2\n\nrows, diag_rows = [], []\nfor qi, g in enumerate(q_order):\n    i1, i2 = top2(C[qi])\n    score, runner = float(C[qi, i1]), float(C[qi, i2])\n    ties = int(((C[qi] >= score - TIE_DR) & (np.arange(len(ref_genes)) != i1)).sum())\n    rows.append({\n        \"target_gene\": ref_genes[i1],\n        \"query_guide_id\": g,\n        \"score\": round(score, 4),\n        \"runner_up_score\": round(runner, 4),\n        \"confidence\": round(score - runner, 4),\n    })\n    diag_rows.append({\n        \"query_guide_id\": g, \"n_cells\": q_ns[g],\n        \"best_gene\": ref_genes[i1], \"score\": score,\n        \"runner_up_gene\": ref_genes[i2], \"runner_up_score\": runner,\n        \"margin\": score - runner, \"near_ties\": ties,\n        \"low_n\": q_ns[g] < LOW_N,\n        \"top5\": [{\"gene\": ref_genes[j], \"r\": round(float(C[qi, j]), 4)}\n                 for j in np.argsort(C[qi])[::-1][:5]],\n    })\n\n# ------------------------------------------------- permutation null (max-r)\nprint(f\"[6] Permutation null: {N_PERM} gene-axis shuffles per guide ...\")\nrng = np.random.default_rng(RNG_SEED)\npvals = []\nfor qi in range(len(q_order)):\n    null_max = np.empty(N_PERM)\n    for b in range(N_PERM):\n        qp = Q[qi][rng.permutation(K_FEATURES)]\n        null_max[b] = pearson_rows(qp[None, :], R)[0].max()\n    pvals.append(float((1 + (null_max >= C[qi].max()).sum()) / (1 + N_PERM)))\nfor d, p in zip(diag_rows, pvals):\n    d[\"perm_pvalue\"] = p\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------- validation\nprint(\"[7] Validation: subsample stability (80% cells) + Spearman variant ...\")\n\ndef build_all(sub_q, sub_r):\n    \"\"\"Rebuild feature-restricted signature matrices from subsampled data.\"\"\"\n    qx = log1p_cpm(sub_q.X); rx = log1p_cpm(sub_r.X)\n    ql = sub_q.obs[\"guide\"].astype(str).values\n    rl = sub_r.obs[\"guide\"].astype(str).values\n    tg = sub_r.obs[\"target_gene\"].astype(str).values\n    qnt = qx[np.array([is_nt(x) for x in ql])].mean(axis=0)\n    rnt = rx[np.array([is_nt(x) for x in rl])].mean(axis=0)\n    qs, qn, qo = signatures(qx, ql, qnt)\n    rs_g, rn, rgo = signatures(rx, rl, rnt)\n    gog = dict(zip(sub_r.obs[\"guide\"].astype(str), tg))\n    rgs = sorted(t for t in set(tg) if t != \"NT\")\n    rs = {t: np.mean([rs_g[g] for g in rgo if gog[g] == t], axis=0) for t in rgs}\n    Ssol = [t for t in rgs\n            if max(rn[g] for g in rgo if gog[g] == t) >= min_ref_n]\n    Sv = np.vstack([rs[t] for t in Ssol]).var(axis=0)\n    fi = np.argsort(Sv)[::-1][:K_FEATURES]\n    return (np.vstack([qs[g][fi] for g in qo]), np.vstack([rs[t][fi] for t in rgs]),\n            qo, rgs, qn)\n\nrng2 = np.random.default_rng(RNG_SEED)\nq_idx = rng2.choice(q.n_obs, size=int(0.8 * q.n_obs), replace=False)\nr_idx = rng2.choice(r.n_obs, size=int(0.8 * r.n_obs), replace=False)\nQs, Rs, qo_s, rg_s, qn_s = build_all(q[q_idx], r[r_idx])\nCs = pearson_rows(Qs, Rs)\nsub_gene = {qo_s[i]: rg_s[int(np.argmax(Cs[i]))] for i in range(len(qo_s))}\nstab = float(np.mean([sub_gene.get(g) == d[\"best_gene\"]\n                      for g, d in zip(q_order, diag_rows)]))\n\ndef spearman(A, B):\n    Ar = np.apply_along_axis(lambda x: x.argsort().argsort().astype(float), 1, A)\n    Br = np.apply_along_axis(lambda x: x.argsort().argsort().astype(float), 1, B)\n    return pearson_rows(Ar, Br)\n\nCsp = spearman(Q, R)\nsp_gene = {q_order[i]: ref_genes[int(np.argmax(Csp[i]))] for i in range(len(q_order))}\nspearman_agree = float(np.mean([sp_gene[g] == d[\"best_gene\"]\n                                for g, d in zip(q_order, diag_rows)]))\nprint(f\"    subsample top-1 stability = {stab:.1%} | \"\n      f\"Spearman top-1 agreement = {spearman_agree:.1%}\")\n\n# raw-profile centroid control: demonstrates cell-type shift breaks naive mapping\nref_centroids = np.vstack([rX[r_gene_lab == t].mean(axis=0) for t in ref_genes])\nraw_best = []\nfor g in q_order:\n    prof = qX[q_lab == g].mean(axis=0)\n    raw_best.append(float(pearson_rows(prof[None, :], ref_centroids)[0].max()))\nraw_best = np.array(raw_best)\nsig_best = np.array([d[\"score\"] for d in diag_rows])\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------- deliverables\ndf = pd.DataFrame(rows).sort_values(\n    \"query_guide_id\", key=lambda s: s.str.replace(\"guide\", \"\").astype(int)\n).reset_index(drop=True)\ndf.to_csv(\"output/guide_mapping.csv\", index=False)\nprint(f\"[8] Wrote output/guide_mapping.csv ({len(df)} guides)\")\n\ngoi = [\"PABPC1\", \"NUDT21\", \"LEO1\"]\nanswers = {t: df.loc[df.target_gene == t, \"query_guide_id\"].tolist() for t in goi}\nprint(\"    guides of interest:\", answers)\n\ndiag = {\n    \"n_common_genes\": int(len(common)),\n    \"n_query_guides\": len(q_order),\n    \"n_ref_genes\": len(ref_genes),\n    \"k_features\": K_FEATURES,\n    \"nt_cells\": {\"query\": int(q_nt_mask.sum()), \"ref\": int(r_nt_mask.sum())},\n    \"nt_vs_nt_profile_r\": round(r_nt_nt, 4),\n    \"subsample_top1_stability\": round(stab, 4),\n    \"spearman_top1_agreement\": round(spearman_agree, 4),\n    \"raw_profile_centroid_max_r\": {\"mean\": round(float(raw_best.mean()), 4),\n                                   \"max\": round(float(raw_best.max()), 4)},\n    \"signature_score_stats\": {\n        \"median_margin\": round(float(np.median(sig_best - np.array([d[\"runner_up_score\"] for d in diag_rows]))), 4),\n        \"min_margin\": round(float(min(d[\"margin\"] for d in diag_rows)), 4),\n        \"median_score\": round(float(np.median(sig_best)), 4),\n    },\n    \"genes_of_interest\": answers,\n    \"per_guide\": diag_rows,\n}\nwith open(\"output/diagnostics.json\", \"w\") as fh:\n    json.dump(diag, fh, indent=1)\nprint(\"    Wrote output/diagnostics.json\")\n\nprint(\"'\"\\\\n=== guide mapping (sorted by guide id) ===\\\")\nprint(df.to_string(index=False))\n'@ | Set-Content -Encoding utf8 output/analysis.py\npython output/analysis.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chenyuqiong\\\\.cache\\\\codex-runtimes\\\\codex-primary-runtime\\\\dependencies\\\\native\\\\powershell\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path output | Out-Null\n@'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\nMap query Perturb-seq perturbation groups to the labeled reference across a\ncell-type shift, and identify query guide IDs targeting PABPC1, NUDT21, LEO1.\n\nPrimary method\n--------------\nThe query and reference live in different cell states (PC1 separation ~10 SD),\nso raw-expression nearest-centroid mapping confounds perturbation identity with\ndataset identity. We therefore map NT-referenced perturbation signatures:\n\n  1. Align query and reference to their common genes.\n  2. Normalize each cell: total-count normalize to 10k, log1p.\n  3. Per dataset, compute the NT baseline = mean log1p-CPM profile over all\n     NT-* (non-targeting control) cells.\n  4. Guide-level signature = mean profile of the guide's cells minus the\n     same-dataset NT baseline (removes dataset/cell-type mean state).\n  5. Reference signatures are aggregated to target_gene level (mean over the\n     gene's guide signatures).\n  6. Features: top-K genes ranked by variance across reference gene-level\n     signatures (feature selection uses ONLY labeled-reference information).\n  7. score(query guide, ref gene) = Pearson r between signatures on K features.\n     score = best r, runner_up_score = second-best r, confidence = margin.\n\nTarget-metadata leakage prevention\n----------------------------------\n  * The only query metadata read is the \"'`guide` column, used solely as a\n    grouping key. We assert the query has no target-gene column.\n  * We assert no query guide ID lexically matches any reference gene symbol\n    (no string-matching shortcut is possible or used).\n  * Reference target_gene is used only to aggregate reference signatures and\n    to report final labels; it never influences query-side computation.\n  * No joint embedding / label transfer; mapping is purely signature-based.\n\nAmbiguity quantification\n------------------------\n  * confidence margin (score - runner_up_score),\n  * empirical p-value per guide from a gene-axis permutation null (B=200) of\n    the max-correlation statistic,\n  * near-tie count (# ref genes within dr=0.02 of the top score),\n  * low-cell-number flag (n < 10).\n\nLightweight validation (one pass)\n---------------------------------\n  * Subsample stability: rebuild signatures from 80% of cells per group\n    (fixed seed) and report top-1 retention across query guides.\n  * Metric robustness: Spearman variant of the same pipeline, top-1 agreement.\n  * Positive/sanity controls: NT-vs-NT profile correlation, and a raw-profile\n    centroid control demonstrating the cell-type shift breaks naive mapping.\n\nOutputs: output/guide_mapping.csv, output/diagnostics.json, stdout summary.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport os\nimport warnings\n\nimport anndata as ad\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport scanpy as sc\n\nwarnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\")\nRNG_SEED = 0\nK_FEATURES = 1500\nN_PERM = 200\nTIE_DR = 0.02\nLOW_N = 10\n\nos.makedirs(\"output\", exist_ok=True)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------- utils\ndef pearson_rows(A, B):\n    \"\"\"Pairwise Pearson r between rows of A (n x p) and rows of B (m x p).\"\"\"\n    A = A - A.mean(axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    B = B - B.mean(axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    An = A / (np.linalg.norm(A, axis=1, keepdims=True) + 1e-12)\n    Bn = B / (np.linalg.norm(B, axis=1, keepdims=True) + 1e-12)\n    return An @ Bn.T\n\n\ndef log1p_cpm(X):\n    s = np.asarray(X.sum(axis=1)).ravel()\n    s[s == 0] = 1.0\n    return np.log1p(np.asarray(X) * (1e4 / s[:, None]))\n\n\ndef is_nt(label):\n    return str(label).startswith(\"NT\")\n\n\ndef signatures(counts, labels, nt_baseline):\n    \"\"\"Mean log1p-CPM signature per non-NT group, referenced to nt_baseline.\"\"\"\n    sigs, ns, order = {}, {}, []\n    lab = np.asarray(labels)\n    for g in pd.unique(lab):\n        if is_nt(g):\n            continue\n        m = counts[lab == g].mean(axis=0)\n        sigs[g] = m - nt_baseline\n        ns[g] = int((lab == g).sum())\n        order.append(g)\n    return sigs, ns, order\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------ load data\nprint(\"[1] Loading data ...\")\nq = ad.read_h5ad(\"inputs/perturb.seq.align.q1.query.h5ad\")\nr = ad.read_h5ad(\"inputs/perturb.seq.align.q1.ref.h5ad\")\n\n# --- leakage guard 1: query metadata must carry no target-gene information\nassert list(q.obs.columns) == [\"guide\"], \"unexpected query metadata columns\"\nassert \"target_gene\" not in q.obs.columns\nq_gene_symbols = {str(g) for g in q.obs[\"guide\"].unique() if not is_nt(g)}\nr_genes = set(r.obs[\"target_gene\"].cat.categories) - {\"NT\"}\noverlap = q_gene_symbols & r_genes | {\n    g for g in q_gene_symbols for t in r_genes if t.lower() in g.lower()\n}\nassert not overlap, f\"query guide IDs lexically reveal targets: {overlap}\"\nprint(f\"    leakage guard OK: query guides are anonymized \"\n      f\"({len(q_gene_symbols)} guides, no symbol overlap with reference)\")\n\ncommon = q.var_names.intersection(r.var_names)\nprint(f\"    common genes: {len(common)}\")\nq = q[:, common].copy()\nr = r[:, common].copy()\n\nqX = log1p_cpm(q.X)\nrX = log1p_cpm(r.X)\nq_lab = q.obs[\"guide\"].astype(str).values\nr_lab = r.obs[\"guide\"].astype(str).values\nr_gene_lab = r.obs[\"target_gene\"].astype(str).values\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------- NT baselines per set\nq_nt_mask = np.array([is_nt(x) for x in q_lab])\nr_nt_mask = np.array([is_nt(x) for x in r_lab])\nq_nt = qX[q_nt_mask].mean(axis=0)\nr_nt = rX[r_nt_mask].mean(axis=0)\nprint(f\"[2] NT baseline cells: query={q_nt_mask.sum()}, ref={r_nt_mask.sum()}\")\n\n# sanity: NT-vs-NT raw profile correlation (same broad lineage control)\nr_nt_nt = float(np.corrcoef(qX[q_nt_mask].mean(axis=0),\n                            rX[r_nt_mask].mean(axis=0))[0, 1])\nprint(f\"    NT vs NT mean-profile Pearson r = {r_nt_nt:.4f}\")\n\n# ------------------------------------------- guide / gene-level signatures\nq_sigs, q_ns, q_order = signatures(qX, q_lab, q_nt)\nr_guide_sigs, r_guide_ns, r_gorder = signatures(rX, r_lab, r_nt)\n\n# reference: aggregate guide signatures to target_gene level\ngene_of_guide = dict(zip(r.obs[\"guide\"].astype(str), r_gene_lab))\nref_genes = sorted(t for t in set(r_gene_lab) if t != \"NT\")\nr_sigs = {}\nfor t in ref_genes:\n    gs = [r_guide_sigs[g] for g in r_gorder if gene_of_guide[g] == t]\n    r_sigs[t] = np.mean(gs, axis=0)\nprint(f\"[3] Signatures: query guides={len(q_order)}, ref genes={len(ref_genes)}\")\n\n# ------------------------------------------- feature selection (ref-only info)\nmin_ref_n = 20\nsolid = [t for t in ref_genes\n         if max(r_guide_ns[g] for g in r_gorder if gene_of_guide[g] == t) >= min_ref_n]\nS = np.vstack([r_sigs[t] for t in solid])\ngene_var = S.var(axis=0)\nfeat_idx = np.argsort(gene_var)[::-1][:K_FEATURES]\nprint(f\"[4] Features: top {K_FEATURES} genes by ref-signature variance \"\n      f\"(using {len(solid)} ref genes with n>={min_ref_n})\")\n\nQ = np.vstack([q_sigs[g][feat_idx] for g in q_order])\nR = np.vstack([r_sigs[t][feat_idx] for t in ref_genes])\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------- scoring\nprint(\"[5] Scoring query guides vs reference gene signatures ...\")\nC = pearson_rows(Q, R)  # n_query x n_genes\n\ndef top2(row):\n    i1 = int(np.argmax(row))\n    row2 = np.delete(row, i1)\n    i2r = int(np.argmax(row2))\n    i2 = i2r if i2r < i1 else i2r + 1\n    return i1, i2\n\nrows, diag_rows = [], []\nfor qi, g in enumerate(q_order):\n    i1, i2 = top2(C[qi])\n    score, runner = float(C[qi, i1]), float(C[qi, i2])\n    ties = int(((C[qi] >= score - TIE_DR) & (np.arange(len(ref_genes)) != i1)).sum())\n    rows.append({\n        \"target_gene\": ref_genes[i1],\n        \"query_guide_id\": g,\n        \"score\": round(score, 4),\n        \"runner_up_score\": round(runner, 4),\n        \"confidence\": round(score - runner, 4),\n    })\n    diag_rows.append({\n        \"query_guide_id\": g, \"n_cells\": q_ns[g],\n        \"best_gene\": ref_genes[i1], \"score\": score,\n        \"runner_up_gene\": ref_genes[i2], \"runner_up_score\": runner,\n        \"margin\": score - runner, \"near_ties\": ties,\n        \"low_n\": q_ns[g] < LOW_N,\n        \"top5\": [{\"gene\": ref_genes[j], \"r\": round(float(C[qi, j]), 4)}\n                 for j in np.argsort(C[qi])[::-1][:5]],\n    })\n\n# ------------------------------------------------- permutation null (max-r)\nprint(f\"[6] Permutation null: {N_PERM} gene-axis shuffles per guide ...\")\nrng = np.random.default_rng(RNG_SEED)\npvals = []\nfor qi in range(len(q_order)):\n    null_max = np.empty(N_PERM)\n    for b in range(N_PERM):\n        qp = Q[qi][rng.permutation(K_FEATURES)]\n        null_max[b] = pearson_rows(qp[None, :], R)[0].max()\n    pvals.append(float((1 + (null_max >= C[qi].max()).sum()) / (1 + N_PERM)))\nfor d, p in zip(diag_rows, pvals):\n    d[\"perm_pvalue\"] = p\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------- validation\nprint(\"[7] Validation: subsample stability (80% cells) + Spearman variant ...\")\n\ndef build_all(sub_q, sub_r):\n    \"\"\"Rebuild feature-restricted signature matrices from subsampled data.\"\"\"\n    qx = log1p_cpm(sub_q.X); rx = log1p_cpm(sub_r.X)\n    ql = sub_q.obs[\"guide\"].astype(str).values\n    rl = sub_r.obs[\"guide\"].astype(str).values\n    tg = sub_r.obs[\"target_gene\"].astype(str).values\n    qnt = qx[np.array([is_nt(x) for x in ql])].mean(axis=0)\n    rnt = rx[np.array([is_nt(x) for x in rl])].mean(axis=0)\n    qs, qn, qo = signatures(qx, ql, qnt)\n    rs_g, rn, rgo = signatures(rx, rl, rnt)\n    gog = dict(zip(sub_r.obs[\"guide\"].astype(str), tg))\n    rgs = sorted(t for t in set(tg) if t != \"NT\")\n    rs = {t: np.mean([rs_g[g] for g in rgo if gog[g] == t], axis=0) for t in rgs}\n    Ssol = [t for t in rgs\n            if max(rn[g] for g in rgo if gog[g] == t) >= min_ref_n]\n    Sv = np.vstack([rs[t] for t in Ssol]).var(axis=0)\n    fi = np.argsort(Sv)[::-1][:K_FEATURES]\n    return (np.vstack([qs[g][fi] for g in qo]), np.vstack([rs[t][fi] for t in rgs]),\n            qo, rgs, qn)\n\nrng2 = np.random.default_rng(RNG_SEED)\nq_idx = rng2.choice(q.n_obs, size=int(0.8 * q.n_obs), replace=False)\nr_idx = rng2.choice(r.n_obs, size=int(0.8 * r.n_obs), replace=False)\nQs, Rs, qo_s, rg_s, qn_s = build_all(q[q_idx], r[r_idx])\nCs = pearson_rows(Qs, Rs)\nsub_gene = {qo_s[i]: rg_s[int(np.argmax(Cs[i]))] for i in range(len(qo_s))}\nstab = float(np.mean([sub_gene.get(g) == d[\"best_gene\"]\n                      for g, d in zip(q_order, diag_rows)]))\n\ndef spearman(A, B):\n    Ar = np.apply_along_axis(lambda x: x.argsort().argsort().astype(float), 1, A)\n    Br = np.apply_along_axis(lambda x: x.argsort().argsort().astype(float), 1, B)\n    return pearson_rows(Ar, Br)\n\nCsp = spearman(Q, R)\nsp_gene = {q_order[i]: ref_genes[int(np.argmax(Csp[i]))] for i in range(len(q_order))}\nspearman_agree = float(np.mean([sp_gene[g] == d[\"best_gene\"]\n                                for g, d in zip(q_order, diag_rows)]))\nprint(f\"    subsample top-1 stability = {stab:.1%} | \"\n      f\"Spearman top-1 agreement = {spearman_agree:.1%}\")\n\n# raw-profile centroid control: demonstrates cell-type shift breaks naive mapping\nref_centroids = np.vstack([rX[r_gene_lab == t].mean(axis=0) for t in ref_genes])\nraw_best = []\nfor g in q_order:\n    prof = qX[q_lab == g].mean(axis=0)\n    raw_best.append(float(pearson_rows(prof[None, :], ref_centroids)[0].max()))\nraw_best = np.array(raw_best)\nsig_best = np.array([d[\"score\"] for d in diag_rows])\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------- deliverables\ndf = p