(non-negative least squares over the 33 gene signatures) and look at the weights. If guide14 = pure PAF1, then w_PAF1≈1. If it's a mix, the weights spread. Also fit with only the four PAF signatures. Unmixing under correlated templates is unstable, but the pattern is informative. Let me try quickly. Also do the same for guide28, guide23, guide1.\n\nActually, one more powerful idea: **use NT-group-level variance as a noise model and compute per-guide posterior probability over genes**: p(g|t) ∝ exp(r(g,t)/σ_t), where σ_t is estimated from a null… over-complicating.\n\nBounded execution: I'll do one more quick diagnostic (NNLS unmixing + full correlation vector for guide1), then finalize the analysis.py rewrite and report. Let's go."}}
