{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_69","type":"reasoning","text":"All the necessary information is in place. Note the pull view for LEO1: guide14 r=0.335 vs runner-up guide20 r=0.176 — the largest pull margin among all genes relative to noise (0.158). Also PABPC1's pull margin is 0.660−0.369=0.291, and NUDT21 is 0.711−0.606=0.105 (runner-up guide19's 0.606 is high because guide19 is CPSF6… interesting but no problem).\n\nNext, write output/report.md. Structure:\n\n# Perturb-seq Query → Reference Mapping Report\n\n1. Task and data\n2. Cell-type shift (why naive mapping fails)\n3. Method (pipeline steps; leakage prevention; two-stage estimator)\n4. Result: guides of interest (answer table)\n5. Full mapping table\n6. Quantification of ambiguity (global + per-guide + LEO1 case)\n7. Validation and controls\n8. Limitations\n9. Reproducibility\n\nKeep the tables compact. Per-guide table: from CSV + p-values + flags. Alright, let's write it."}}
